## 1. Project Initialization

| Command | When to use it |
|---------|---------------|
| `/gsd:new-project` | **Starting a brand-new project from scratch.** Runs questioning → research → requirements → roadmap. Creates `.planning/PROJECT.md`, `REQUIREMENTS.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `STATE.md`. Use on Day 1 of a greenfield project. |
| `/gsd:new-milestone` | **Starting a new milestone within an existing project.** Equivalent to new-project but preserves PROJECT.md history. Use when you've completed a milestone and are beginning the next (e.g., v1.0 done, starting v1.1). |
| `/gsd:onboard` | **Bringing an existing codebase into GSD.** Brownfield projects — maps the codebase, ingests existing docs, sets up `.planning/`, produces an onboarding summary. Use when you inherit a project that has code but no `.planning/` folder. |
| `/gsd:import` | **Importing an external plan file** (e.g., a PRD from another tool) into GSD with conflict detection against existing PROJECT.md decisions. Use `--from <filepath>` for files, `--from-gsd2` to reverse-migrate a GSD v2 project. |
| `/gsd:ingest-docs` | **Bootstrapping `.planning/` from multiple existing documents** (ADRs, PRDs, SPECs) in one pass. Auto-synthesizes conflicts using precedence `ADR > SPEC > PRD > DOC`. Use when you have a folder of planning docs and want GSD to ingest them all. |
| `/gsd:map-codebase` | **Analyzing an existing codebase** with parallel mapper agents to produce 7 structured documents in `.planning/codebase/` (STACK, ARCHITECTURE, STRUCTURE, CONVENTIONS, TESTING, INTEGRATIONS, CONCERNS). Use before onboarding or after significant refactoring. |

