## 2. Phase Pipeline — The Core Build Loop

This is the main execution path. Every feature goes through this cycle per phase:

```
discuss-phase → spec-phase → plan-phase → execute-phase → verify-work
```

| Command | When to use it |
|---------|---------------|
| `/gsd:discuss-phase <N>` | **Before planning a phase.** Gathers implementation decisions through adaptive questioning. Produces `<N>-CONTEXT.md` so downstream agents don't need to ask you again. Use at the start of every phase. |
| `/gsd:spec-phase <N>` | **Clarifying WHAT a phase delivers** before discuss-phase. Socratic questioning with ambiguity scoring. Produces SPEC.md with falsifiable requirements. Use when requirements are ambiguous or you want measurable acceptance criteria. |
| `/gsd:plan-phase <N>` | **Creating PLAN.md** for a phase. Researches domain, spawns planner, verifies with plan-checker, iterates until pass. Use after discuss-phase produces acceptable CONTEXT.md. |
| `/gsd:execute-phase <N>` | **Running all plans in a phase** with wave-based parallel execution via subagents. Use when PLAN.md files are ready. Optional `--wave N` to run one wave at a time, `--gaps-only` for fix plans, `--interactive` for pair-programming style. |
| `/gsd:verify-work <N>` | **Validating built features** through conversational UAT. Tests one at a time, plain text. Produces `<N>-UAT.md`. Use after execute-phase completes. |
| `/gsd:validate-phase <N>` | **Auditing Nyquist validation gaps** for a completed phase. Produces VALIDATION.md + test files. Use when you need deep validation coverage beyond UAT. |
| `/gsd:add-tests <N>` | **Generating unit and E2E tests** for a completed phase based on SUMMARY.md, CONTEXT.md, VERIFICATION.md. Uses RED-GREEN conventions. Use after verify-work passes. |
| `/gsd:autonomous` | **Running all remaining phases with no human in the loop.** Discuss → plan → execute per phase. Pauses only for user decisions. Use when you want the agent to drive an entire milestone end-to-end. |
| `/gsd:mvp-phase <N>` | **Planning a phase as a vertical MVP slice.** Prompts for user story, runs SPIDR splitting check, writes mode=MVP to ROADMAP.md. Use for Day 1-style vertical feature slices. |
| `/gsd:plan-review-convergence <N>` | **Cross-AI plan convergence loop.** Repeatedly: plan-phase → external AI review → replan → re-review until no unresolved concerns. Use for critical phases where you want multiple AI perspectives. |
| `/gsd:ultraplan-phase <N>` | **Offload planning to Claude Code's ultraplan cloud.** Beta. Use when local planning is too expensive and you have a Claude Code subscription. |
| `/gsd:phase` | **Managing phases in ROADMAP.md** — add, insert, remove, or edit phases. Use `--insert` for urgent work as decimal phase (e.g., 72.1), `--remove` to delete a future phase, `--edit` to modify phase fields. |

