## 5. Milestone & Project Management

| Command | When to use it |
|---------|---------------|
| `/gsd:complete-milestone <version>` | **Archiving a completed milestone.** Verifies requirements, gathers stats, extracts accomplishments, archives to `.planning/milestones/`, updates PROJECT.md, tags git. Use when all phases in a milestone are done. |
| `/gsd:milestone-summary <version>` | **Generating a comprehensive project summary** for team onboarding and review. Produces MILESTONE_SUMMARY.md. Use when documenting what was shipped. |
| `/gsd:progress` | **Checking project progress** — shows status, summarizes recent work, intelligently routes to the next action. Subcommands: `--next` (auto-advance), `--do "task"` (smart dispatch), `--forensic` (integrity audit). Use frequently to stay oriented. |
| `/gsd:stats` | **Displaying project statistics** — phases, plans, requirements, git metrics, timeline. Use for status reports or checking how much work remains. |
| `/gsd:manager` | **Interactive command center** for managing multiple phases from one terminal. Shows dashboard, recommends next actions, dispatches work. Use for power users managing parallel work. |
| `/gsd:workstreams` | **Managing parallel workstreams** — list, create, switch, status, progress, complete, resume. Use when working on multiple independent features/milestones simultaneously. |
| `/gsd:next` | **Smart entry point.** Detects project state, presents a menu of the right next action, dispatches to it. Use when you're not sure what to do next. |

