## 6. Session & Context Management

| Command | When to use it |
|---------|---------------|
| `/gsd:pause-work` | **Creating a context handoff** when pausing mid-phase. Creates `.continue-here.md` with complete state, commits as WIP. Use when you need to stop mid-session. |
| `/gsd:resume-work` | **Resuming from a previous session.** Restores STATE.md, detects checkpoints, finds incomplete work, routes to next action. Use when starting a new session. |
| `/gsd:thread` | **Managing persistent context threads** for cross-session work that doesn't belong to a specific phase. Use for ongoing investigations or topics spanning multiple sessions. |
| `/gsd:health` | **Diagnosing planning directory health.** Checks for missing files, invalid configs, inconsistent state. Use `--repair` to auto-fix, `--context` to check context utilization. |
| `/gsd:undo` | **Safe git revert** of phase or plan commits. Uses phase manifest with dependency checks. Modes: `--last N`, `--phase NN`, `--plan NN-MM`. Use when you need to roll back GSD artifacts. |
| `/gsd:debug` | **Systematic debugging** with persistent state across context resets. Subcommands: `list`, `status <slug>`, `continue <slug>`, `--diagnose`. Use when a feature doesn't work as expected. |
| `/gsd:forensics` | **Post-mortem investigation** for failed GSD workflows. Analyzes git history, planning artifacts, produces structured diagnostic report. Use when a workflow broke and you need to understand why. |
| `/gsd:surface` | **Managing which skills are surfaced** — apply a profile, list, disable/enable clusters. Use to control which GSD capabilities are visible in your agent. |
| `/gsd:settings` | **Configuring GSD workflow toggles** and model profile. Use to set research/plan-check/verifier preferences, code review depth, worktree settings, etc. |
| `/gsd:update` | **Updating GSD to latest version.** Shows changelog, installs if available. Use `--sync` for multi-runtime sync, `--reapply` for restoring customizations after update. |

