## 7. Infrastructure & Operations

| Command | When to use it |
|---------|---------------|
| `/gsd:docs-update` | **Generating/updating project documentation** verified against the codebase. Produces up to 9 doc files. Use `--force` to regenerate all, `--verify-only` to check accuracy without writing. |
| `/gsd:graphify` | **Building/querying the project knowledge graph** in `.planning/graphs/`. Modes: `build`, `query <term>`, `status`, `diff`. Use for understanding codebase relationships or querying project knowledge. |
| `/gsd:mempalace-recall` | **Recalling prior decisions, patterns, and surprises** from MemPalace before planning. Read-only. Use before discuss-phase to leverage historical context. |
| `/gsd:mempalace-capture` | **Filing phase artifacts into MemPalace** with temporal KG mirroring. Use after completing a phase to preserve institutional knowledge. |
| `/gsd:pr-branch` | **Creating a clean PR branch** by filtering out `.planning/` commits. Reviewers see only code changes. Use when preparing code for peer review. |
| `/gsd:inbox` | **Triaging GitHub issues and PRs** against project templates. Use for open-source projects with active GitHub inboxes. |
| `/gsd:workspace` | **Managing isolated workspaces** — create, list, remove. Use for parallel work in clean environments. |

